(function(){
  try {
    if (typeof QB === 'undefined' || !Array.isArray(QB)) { if(window.console) console.warn('[qbank-elec] QB no disponible'); return; }
    window.QB_ELEC = [{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-GEN-001","es":{"q":"¿Qué tipo de red eléctrica genera de forma normal el sistema del A320?","keys":["corriente","alterna","trifasica","115","200","400"],"answer":"En configuración normal la red primaria es AC trifásica 115/200 V 400 Hz de frecuencia constante, y una parte se convierte en 28 V DC para ciertas aplicaciones. La red DC no es la fuente primaria: se obtiene a partir de la AC mediante los TR. (FCOM DSC-24-10-10 · p. 5 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Corriente alterna trifásica 115/200 V 400 Hz de frecuencia constante, más una red de 28 V DC","Corriente continua de 28 V como fuente primaria, invertida a AC cuando hace falta","Corriente alterna monofásica 115 V de frecuencia variable, más 24 V DC","Corriente alterna trifásica 230/400 V 50 Hz, más 28 V DC"]},"en":{"q":"What type of electrical network does the A320 system normally generate?","keys":["three","phase","115","200","400","constant"],"answer":"In normal configuration the primary network is three-phase 115/200 V 400 Hz constant-frequency AC, and part of it is converted into 28 V DC for certain applications. DC is not the primary source: it is derived from AC through the TRs. (FCOM DSC-24-10-10 · p. 5 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Three-phase 115/200 V 400 Hz constant-frequency AC, plus a 28 V DC network","28 V DC as the primary source, inverted to AC when required","Single-phase 115 V variable-frequency AC, plus 24 V DC","Three-phase 230/400 V 50 Hz AC, plus 28 V DC"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-ACG-001","es":{"q":"¿Cuántos generadores forman la red eléctrica en configuración normal y quién los acciona?","keys":["generadores","motor","generador","apu","constituida","gen"],"answer":"La red está constituida por 2 generadores de motor (GEN 1 y GEN 2), accionados cada uno por su motor mediante un accionamiento integrado, y 1 generador de APU. Cada generador puede alimentar todas las barras. El de emergencia sólo entra si fallan los principales. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["2 generadores de motor (uno por motor) y 1 generador de APU","1 generador de motor y 2 generadores de APU","3 generadores de motor, sin generador de APU","2 generadores de motor y el generador de emergencia siempre en línea"]},"en":{"q":"How many generators make up the network in normal configuration and what drives them?","keys":["engine","generators","apu","generator","network","gen"],"answer":"The network is made up of 2 engine generators (GEN 1 and GEN 2), each driven by its engine through an integrated drive, and 1 APU generator. Each generator can supply all busbars. The emergency generator only comes in if the main ones fail. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["2 engine generators (one per engine) and 1 APU generator","1 engine generator and 2 APU generators","3 engine generators, no APU generator","2 engine generators and the emergency generator always on line"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-ACG-002","es":{"q":"¿Dónde se conecta la energía eléctrica externa (GPU) al avión?","keys":["conector","tierra","situado","cerca","rueda","morro"],"answer":"El conector de energía de tierra está cerca de la rueda de morro y permite alimentar todas las barras. Es una fuente AC más, gestionada por el GPCU/GAPCU, con prioridad por encima del APU cuando el EXT PWR pb está en ON. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["En un conector de tierra situado cerca de la rueda de morro","En un conector situado en la cola, junto al APU","En cada góndola de motor, uno por lado","En el compartimento de aviónica, bajo el suelo de cabina"]},"en":{"q":"Where is external electrical power (GPU) connected to the aircraft?","keys":["ground","power","connector","located","nosewheel","allows"],"answer":"The ground power connector is near the nosewheel and allows all busbars to be supplied. It is another AC source, managed by the GPCU/GAPCU, with priority over the APU when the EXT PWR pb is ON. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["At a ground power connector located near the nosewheel","At a connector on the tail, next to the APU","At each engine nacelle, one per side","In the avionics compartment, under the cockpit floor"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-BAT-001","es":{"q":"¿Cuántas baterías principales tiene el avión y a qué barras están conectadas de forma permanente?","keys":["baterias","conectadas","forma","permanente","buses","principales"],"answer":"Hay 2 baterías principales conectadas permanentemente a las dos hot buses; por eso las hot buses nunca se quedan sin alimentación. Cada batería tiene su Battery Charge Limiter (BCL), que gestiona la conexión al DC BAT BUS según la necesidad de carga. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["2 baterías, conectadas de forma permanente a las dos hot buses","1 batería, conectada al DC BAT BUS","3 baterías, una por cada TR","2 baterías, conectadas al DC ESS BUS"]},"en":{"q":"How many main batteries does the aircraft have and to which buses are they permanently connected?","keys":["batteries","permanently","connected","buses","there","never"],"answer":"There are 2 main batteries permanently connected to the two hot buses; that is why the hot buses are never left unpowered. Each battery has its Battery Charge Limiter (BCL), which manages connection to the DC BAT BUS depending on charging need. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["2 batteries, permanently connected to the two hot buses","1 battery, connected to the DC BAT BUS","3 batteries, one per TR","2 batteries, connected to the DC ESS BUS"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-GEN-002","es":{"q":"En cuanto a prioridad de suministro, ¿qué carácter tiene la alimentación comercial (galleys, entretenimiento)?","keys":["prioridad","secundaria","primero","desconecta","falta","potencia"],"answer":"La alimentación comercial tiene prioridad secundaria. Por eso, ante la pérdida de un generador, parte del galley y el DC BUS Entertainment se desconectan automáticamente: el sistema protege primero las cargas esenciales de vuelo. (FCOM DSC-24-10-10 · p. 5 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Prioridad secundaria: es lo primero que se desconecta cuando falta potencia","Prioridad máxima, por encima de los sistemas de vuelo","La misma prioridad que las barras esenciales","No tiene relación con la disponibilidad de generadores"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding supply priority, what character does commercial power (galleys, entertainment) have?","keys":["secondary","priority","first","thing","power","short"],"answer":"Commercial supply has secondary priority. That is why, on loss of a generator, part of the galley and the DC BUS Entertainment are shed automatically: the system protects essential flight loads first. (FCOM DSC-24-10-10 · p. 5 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Secondary priority: it is the first thing shed when power is short","Highest priority, above flight systems","The same priority as the essential buses","No relation to generator availability"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-EMER-001","es":{"q":"¿Qué acciona el generador de emergencia del A320?","keys":["circuito","hidraulico","traves","motor","acciona","generador"],"answer":"El circuito hidráulico azul acciona el generador de emergencia mediante un motor hidráulico. La RAT es la que presuriza el circuito azul cuando se despliega; de ahí que la velocidad sea clave para mantener el generador de emergencia alimentando. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["El circuito hidráulico azul (blue), a través de un motor hidráulico","Un motor eléctrico alimentado por las baterías","El sistema hidráulico verde a través de la PTU","Directamente el APU"]},"en":{"q":"What drives the A320 emergency generator?","keys":["hydraulic","circuit","through","motor","drives","emergency"],"answer":"The blue hydraulic circuit drives the emergency generator through a hydraulic motor. The RAT is what pressurizes the blue circuit when deployed; hence airspeed is key to keep the emergency generator supplying. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["The blue hydraulic circuit, through a hydraulic motor","An electric motor powered by the batteries","The green hydraulic system through the PTU","The APU directly"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-DIST-001","es":{"q":"¿Pueden acoplarse en paralelo los generadores del A320?","keys":["generadores","conectarse","paralelo","nunca","acoplan","alimenta"],"answer":"Los generadores nunca se acoplan en paralelo: cada uno alimenta su canal y los contactores de barra (BTC) reparten la red sin unir salidas. Por eso un solo generador puede alimentar toda la red, pero repartiéndola, no sumando potencias. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-10 · p. 11 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["No, los generadores no pueden conectarse en paralelo","Sí, GEN 1 y GEN 2 trabajan siempre en paralelo","Sólo en tierra con el APU","Sólo el generador de emergencia con las baterías"]},"en":{"q":"Can the A320 generators be connected in parallel?","keys":["generators","cannot","connected","parallel","never","paralleled"],"answer":"The generators are never paralleled: each supplies its channel and the bus tie contactors (BTC) split the network without joining outputs. That is why a single generator can supply the whole network, but by distribution, not by adding power. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-10 · p. 11 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["No, the generators cannot be connected in parallel","Yes, GEN 1 and GEN 2 always work in parallel","Only on ground with the APU","Only the emergency generator with the batteries"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CB-001","es":{"q":"¿Por qué llevan un capuchón rojo los circuit breakers del Wing Tip Brake (WTB)?","keys":["impedir","rearmen","reset","capuchon","impide","rearme"],"answer":"El capuchón rojo del WTB impide su rearme: rearmar ese C/B podría reactivar los frenos de punta de ala en un momento inadecuado. Es una salvaguarda física, no una indicación de monitorización. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 15 FEB 11)","opts":["Para impedir que se rearmen (reset)","Para indicar que son monitorizados por el ECAM","Porque alimentan cargas de emergencia","Para señalar que están normalmente abiertos"]},"en":{"q":"Why do the Wing Tip Brake (WTB) circuit breakers have a red cap?","keys":["prevent","being","reset","prevents","resetting","could"],"answer":"The WTB red cap prevents resetting: resetting that C/B could reactivate the wing tip brakes at the wrong moment and damage the system. It is a physical safeguard against inadvertent action, not a monitoring indication; monitoring is the separate role of the green C/Bs. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 15 FEB 11)","opts":["To prevent them from being reset","To indicate they are ECAM-monitored","Because they feed emergency loads","To show they are normally open"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-IND-001","es":{"q":"En el MEMO del E/WD, ¿qué indica el mensaje verde 'EMER GEN'?","keys":["generador","emergencia","marcha","running","emer","gen"],"answer":"El MEMO 'EMER GEN' aparece en verde cuando el generador de emergencia está en marcha. Un fallo se señalaría con la luz FAULT roja del panel y las alertas ECAM correspondientes, no con el MEMO verde. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 49 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Que el generador de emergencia está en marcha (running)","Que el generador de emergencia ha fallado","Que la RAT está armada pero no desplegada","Que las baterías están alimentando las ESS BUS"]},"en":{"q":"On the E/WD MEMO, what does the green 'EMER GEN' message indicate?","keys":["emergency","generator","running","emer","gen","appears"],"answer":"The 'EMER GEN' MEMO appears green when the emergency generator is running. A failure would be shown by the red FAULT light on the panel and the corresponding ECAM alerts, not by the green MEMO. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 49 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["That the emergency generator is running","That the emergency generator has failed","That the RAT is armed but not deployed","That the batteries are supplying the ESS buses"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-ACG-003","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la función de las Generator Control Units (GCU) de los generadores de motor?","keys":["controlar","frecuencia","tension","salida","proteger","mediante"],"answer":"Cada GCU controla la frecuencia y la tensión de salida de su generador y protege la red controlando el line contactor asociado. La conversión AC→DC la hacen los TR, no la GCU. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Controlar frecuencia y tensión de salida y proteger la red mediante el line contactor","Arrancar y parar el motor asociado","Regular sólo la temperatura del IDG","Convertir la AC en DC para las barras esenciales"]},"en":{"q":"What is the function of the engine generators' Generator Control Units (GCU)?","keys":["control","output","frequency","voltage","protect","network"],"answer":"Each GCU controls the frequency and voltage of its generator's output and protects the network by controlling the associated line contactor. AC→DC conversion is done by the TRs, not the GCU. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Control output frequency and voltage and protect the network via the line contactor","Start and stop the associated engine","Regulate only the IDG temperature","Convert AC into DC for the essential buses"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-ACG-004","es":{"q":"¿Qué capacidad tiene el generador de APU respecto a los generadores de motor?","keys":["produce","misma","salida","generador","motor","sustituir"],"answer":"El generador de APU, accionado directamente por el APU, produce la misma salida que cada generador de motor y puede sustituir a uno o a ambos en cualquier momento, en tierra o en vuelo. Por eso arrancar el APU es una opción válida para recuperar red ante la pérdida de generadores de motor. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Produce la misma salida que un generador de motor y puede sustituir a uno o a ambos en cualquier momento","Produce la mitad de potencia y sólo sirve en tierra","Sólo puede alimentar las barras esenciales","Sólo sustituye a un generador de motor y únicamente por debajo de 100 kt"]},"en":{"q":"What capability does the APU generator have relative to the engine generators?","keys":["produces","output","engine","generator","replace","either"],"answer":"The APU generator, driven directly by the APU, produces the same output as each engine generator and can replace either or both at any time, on ground or in flight. That is why starting the APU is a valid option to recover the network on loss of engine generators. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["It produces the same output as an engine generator and can replace either or both at any time","It produces half the power and is only usable on ground","It can only supply the essential buses","It can only replace one engine generator and only below 100 kt"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-ACG-005","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la potencia y las características de salida de cada generador de motor?","keys":["90","kva","trifasico","115","200","400"],"answer":"Cada generador de motor entrega hasta 90 KVA de potencia trifásica 115/200 V 400 Hz. Cuidado con confundirlo: 5 KVA es el generador de emergencia y 200 A es la salida DC de cada TR. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["90 KVA, trifásico 115/200 V 400 Hz","45 KVA, monofásico 115 V 400 Hz","5 KVA, trifásico 115/200 V 400 Hz","200 A, 28 V DC"]},"en":{"q":"What is the output rating and characteristics of each engine generator?","keys":["90","kva","three","phase","115","200"],"answer":"Each engine generator delivers up to 90 KVA of three-phase 115/200 V 400 Hz power. Beware confusing it: 5 KVA is the emergency generator and 200 A is the DC output of each TR. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["90 KVA, three-phase 115/200 V 400 Hz","45 KVA, single-phase 115 V 400 Hz","5 KVA, three-phase 115/200 V 400 Hz","200 A, 28 V DC"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-EMER-002","es":{"q":"¿Cuánta potencia entrega el generador de emergencia y de qué tipo?","keys":["kva","trifasicos","115","200","400","generador"],"answer":"El generador de emergencia entrega 5 KVA trifásicos a 115 y 200 V 400 Hz, suficientes para las barras esenciales. El static inverter (1 KVA monofásico) es la otra fuente de emergencia, pero mucho más limitada. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["5 KVA trifásicos, 115 y 200 V 400 Hz","1 KVA monofásico, 115 V 400 Hz","90 KVA trifásicos, 115/200 V 400 Hz","28 V DC hasta 200 A"]},"en":{"q":"How much power does the emergency generator deliver and of what type?","keys":["kva","three","phase","115","200","400"],"answer":"The emergency generator delivers 5 KVA three-phase at 115 and 200 V 400 Hz, enough for the essential buses. The static inverter (1 KVA single-phase) is the other emergency source, but much more limited. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["5 KVA three-phase, 115 and 200 V 400 Hz","1 KVA single-phase, 115 V 400 Hz","90 KVA three-phase, 115/200 V 400 Hz","28 V DC up to 200 A"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-SINV-001","es":{"q":"¿Qué hace el static inverter y de dónde toma la energía?","keys":["transforma","bat","kva","monofasica","115","400"],"answer":"El static inverter transforma la DC de la BATERÍA 1 en 1 KVA de AC monofásica 115 V 400 Hz que alimenta parte del AC ESS BUS. Es la última red AC disponible cuando ni siquiera el generador de emergencia está presente. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Transforma DC de la BAT 1 en 1 KVA de AC monofásica 115 V 400 Hz para parte del AC ESS BUS","Convierte AC del generador de emergencia en DC para el DC ESS BUS","Carga las baterías a partir del bus DC BAT","Transforma DC de ambas baterías en 5 KVA de AC trifásica"]},"en":{"q":"What does the static inverter do and where does it take its power from?","keys":["transforms","bat","kva","single","phase","115"],"answer":"The static inverter transforms BATTERY 1 DC into 1 KVA of single-phase 115 V 400 Hz AC that supplies part of the AC ESS BUS. It is the last AC network available when not even the emergency generator is present. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Transforms BAT 1 DC into 1 KVA of single-phase 115 V 400 Hz AC for part of the AC ESS BUS","Converts emergency-generator AC into DC for the DC ESS BUS","Charges the batteries from the DC BAT bus","Transforms both batteries' DC into 5 KVA of three-phase AC"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-DCG-001","es":{"q":"¿Cuántos TR principales alimentan el sistema DC y con qué corriente máxima?","keys":["200","principales","alimentan","existe","ademas","ess"],"answer":"Dos TR principales, TR 1 y TR 2, alimentan la red DC con hasta 200 A. Existe además el ESS TR (idéntico) para el circuito DC esencial y un TR Entertainment para el IFE. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Dos TR (TR 1 y TR 2), hasta 200 A cada uno","Un único TR de 400 A","Tres TR de 90 A cada uno","Dos TR de 23 A cada uno"]},"en":{"q":"How many main TRs supply the DC system and at what maximum current?","keys":["200","supply","network","there","ess","identical"],"answer":"Two main TRs, TR 1 and TR 2, supply the DC network with up to 200 A. There is also the ESS TR (identical) for the essential DC circuit and a TR Entertainment for the IFE. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Two TRs (TR 1 and TR 2), up to 200 A each","A single 400 A TR","Three TRs of 90 A each","Two TRs of 23 A each"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-BAT-002","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la capacidad nominal de cada batería principal del A320?","keys":["23","bateria","principal","tiene","capacidad","nominal"],"answer":"Cada batería principal tiene una capacidad nominal de 23 Ah. Es el dato que dimensiona la autonomía en configuración de baterías, junto con las cargas realmente conectadas a las ESS BUS. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["23 Ah","5 Ah","40 Ah","15 Ah"]},"en":{"q":"What is the normal capacity of each A320 main battery?","keys":["23","battery","normal","capacity","figure","sizes"],"answer":"Each main battery has a normal capacity of 23 Ah. This figure sizes the endurance in battery-only configuration, together with the loads actually connected to the ESS buses. It is why prolonged flight on batteries alone is not recommended. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["23 Ah","5 Ah","40 Ah","15 Ah"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-DCG-002","es":{"q":"¿Qué función cumple el Battery Charge Limiter (BCL) de cada batería?","keys":["vigila","carga","bateria","controla","contactor","linea"],"answer":"El BCL vigila el proceso de carga y controla el contactor de la batería: la conecta al DC BAT BUS cuando necesita carga y la desconecta cuando está plena. También la conecta en los casos automáticos (arranque de APU, pérdida de AC BUS a baja velocidad). (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Vigila la carga de la batería y controla su contactor de línea","Convierte la DC de la batería en AC para el AC ESS","Regula la temperatura de la batería","Selecciona qué TR alimenta el DC BAT BUS"]},"en":{"q":"What is the function of each battery's Battery Charge Limiter (BCL)?","keys":["monitors","battery","charging","controls","contactor","process"],"answer":"The BCL monitors the charging process and controls the battery contactor: it connects the battery to the DC BAT BUS when it needs charging and disconnects it when full. It also connects it in the automatic cases (APU start, loss of AC BUS at low speed). (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Monitors battery charging and controls its battery contactor","Converts battery DC into AC for the AC ESS","Regulates the battery temperature","Selects which TR supplies the DC BAT BUS"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CB-002","es":{"q":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre un circuit breaker monitorizado (verde) y uno no monitorizado (negro)?","keys":["verde","queda","abierto","dispara","advertencia","tripped"],"answer":"El C/B monitorizado (verde), cuando permanece abierto más de 1 minuto, dispara la advertencia C/B TRIPPED en el ECAM indicando el panel afectado. El no monitorizado (negro) no genera esa alerta. El color no indica amperaje ni tipo de corriente. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 15 FEB 11)","opts":["El verde, si queda abierto más de 1 min, dispara la advertencia C/B TRIPPED en el ECAM; el negro no se monitoriza","El verde es de mayor amperaje que el negro","El negro alimenta cargas AC y el verde cargas DC","El verde no puede rearmarse y el negro sí"]},"en":{"q":"What is the difference between a monitored (green) and a non-monitored (black) circuit breaker?","keys":["green","triggers","tripped","warning","ecam","black"],"answer":"The monitored (green) C/B, when left out for more than 1 minute, triggers the C/B TRIPPED warning on ECAM indicating the affected panel. The non-monitored (black) one produces no such alert. Colour indicates neither rating nor current type. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 15 FEB 11)","opts":["The green, if left out for more than 1 min, triggers the C/B TRIPPED warning on ECAM; the black is not monitored","The green is higher-rated than the black","The black feeds AC loads and the green feeds DC loads","The green cannot be reset and the black can"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-DIST-002","es":{"q":"¿Qué relación de prioridad hay entre los generadores de motor, el generador de APU y la energía externa?","keys":["generadores","motor","tienen","prioridad","apu","energia"],"answer":"Cuando funcionan, GEN 1 y GEN 2 tienen prioridad sobre el generador de APU y sobre la energía externa. Entre APU y externa, la externa tiene prioridad cuando el EXT PWR pb está en ON. En vuelo, arrancar el APU no 'roba' la red a los generadores de motor. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-10 · p. 11 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Los generadores de motor tienen prioridad sobre el APU y sobre la energía externa","El APU tiene prioridad sobre los generadores de motor","La energía externa tiene prioridad sobre los generadores de motor","Las tres fuentes tienen la misma prioridad y trabajan en paralelo"]},"en":{"q":"What priority relationship is there between engine generators, APU generator and external power?","keys":["engine","generators","priority","apu","external","power"],"answer":"When operating, GEN 1 and GEN 2 have priority over the APU generator and over external power. Between APU and external, external power has priority when the EXT PWR pb is ON. In flight, starting the APU does not 'steal' the network from the engine generators. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-10 · p. 11 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["The engine generators have priority over the APU and over external power","The APU has priority over the engine generators","External power has priority over the engine generators","All three sources have equal priority and work in parallel"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-NORM-001","es":{"q":"En configuración normal en vuelo, ¿qué barra alimenta normalmente el AC ESS BUS?","keys":["bus","traves","contactor","normal","ess","alimenta"],"answer":"En normal, el AC ESS BUS se alimenta del AC BUS 1 mediante un contactor. Si se pierde el AC BUS 1, el AC ESS FEED (auto switching) lo pasa al AC BUS 2. El generador de emergencia y el static inverter sólo entran en configuración de emergencia. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-20 · p. 13 · rev 09 OCT 12)","opts":["El AC BUS 1, a través de un contactor","El AC BUS 2, a través del AC ESS FEED","El generador de emergencia","El static inverter desde la BAT 1"]},"en":{"q":"In normal in-flight configuration, which bus normally supplies the AC ESS BUS?","keys":["bus","through","contactor","normal","ess","switching"],"answer":"In normal, the AC ESS BUS is fed from AC BUS 1 through a contactor. If AC BUS 1 is lost, the AC ESS FEED (auto switching) transfers it to AC BUS 2. The emergency generator and static inverter only come in emergency configuration. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-20 · p. 13 · rev 09 OCT 12)","opts":["AC BUS 1, through a contactor","AC BUS 2, through the AC ESS FEED","The emergency generator","The static inverter from BAT 1"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-EMER-003","es":{"q":"Durante el despliegue de la RAT y el acoplamiento del generador de emergencia (unos 8 s), ¿quién alimenta la red de emergencia?","keys":["baterias","durante","tardan","despliegue","rat","acoplamiento"],"answer":"Durante los ~8 s que tardan el despliegue de la RAT y el acoplamiento del generador de emergencia, son las baterías las que sostienen la red de emergencia. No hay blackout total: por eso las baterías son críticas en esa transición. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["Las baterías","El APU, que arranca automáticamente","Nadie: hay un corte total durante esos segundos","El generador de motor restante"]},"en":{"q":"During RAT extension and emergency generator coupling (about 8 s), who powers the emergency network?","keys":["batteries","during","rat","extension","emergency","generator"],"answer":"During the ~8 s that RAT extension and emergency generator coupling take, the batteries sustain the emergency network. There is no total blackout: that is why the batteries are critical in that transition. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["The batteries","The APU, which starts automatically","Nobody: there is a total blackout for those seconds","The remaining engine generator"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-ABN-001","es":{"q":"Ante el fallo de un generador de motor, ¿cómo reacciona el sistema?","keys":["sustituye","automaticamente","generador","fallido","apu","gen"],"answer":"El sistema reemplaza automáticamente el generador fallido con el APU GEN (si está disponible) o con el otro generador de motor. Además, se desconecta parte del galley y el DC BUS Entertainment. No hace falta desplegar la RAT ni conectar baterías. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 17 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Sustituye automáticamente el generador fallido por el APU GEN si está disponible, o por el otro generador de motor","Despliega la RAT inmediatamente","Conecta las baterías a todas las barras","Exige acción manual del piloto para restablecer la red"]},"en":{"q":"On failure of one engine generator, how does the system react?","keys":["automatically","replaces","failed","generator","apu","gen"],"answer":"The system automatically replaces the failed generator with the APU GEN (if available) or the other engine generator. Part of the galley and the DC BUS Entertainment are also shed. No RAT deployment or battery connection is needed. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 17 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Automatically replaces the failed generator with the APU GEN if available, or the other engine generator","Deploys the RAT immediately","Connects the batteries to all buses","Requires manual pilot action to restore the network"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-IND-002","es":{"q":"En la página ELEC del ECAM, ¿cuándo se vuelve ámbar la indicación de carga (load) de un generador?","keys":["carga","supera","100","potencia","nominal","indicacion"],"answer":"La indicación de carga del generador se vuelve ámbar cuando supera el 100 % de la potencia nominal (sobrecarga). También aparece la luz FAULT del GALLEY pb cuando la carga de cualquier generador supera el 100 %, permitiendo aligerar cargas. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 44 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Cuando la carga supera el 100 % de la potencia nominal","Cuando la carga baja del 50 %","Cuando la tensión baja de 110 V","Sólo con el generador de emergencia en marcha"]},"en":{"q":"On the ECAM ELEC page, when does a generator's load indication become amber?","keys":["exceeds","100","rated","output","generator","indication"],"answer":"The generator load indication becomes amber when it exceeds 100 % of rated output (overload). The GALLEY pb FAULT light also comes on when any generator's load exceeds 100 %, allowing loads to be shed. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 44 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["When the load exceeds 100 % of rated output","When the load drops below 50 %","When the voltage drops below 110 V","Only with the emergency generator running"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-001","es":{"q":"Tras desconectar un IDG desde cabina, ¿quién puede volver a conectarlo?","keys":["personal","mantenimiento","desconexion","idg","accion","sentido"],"answer":"La desconexión del IDG es una acción de sentido único: una vez desconectado del eje, sólo el personal de mantenimiento puede reconectarlo. Por eso la desconexión sólo se ordena cuando el procedimiento lo exige y con el motor girando. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 31 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Sólo el personal de mantenimiento","La tripulación, presionando de nuevo el pb en tierra","Se reconecta solo al apagar y arrancar el motor","Se reconecta automáticamente si la temperatura baja de 180 °C"]},"en":{"q":"After disconnecting an IDG from the cockpit, who can reconnect it?","keys":["maintenance","personnel","idg","disconnection","action","disconnected"],"answer":"IDG disconnection is a one-way action: once disconnected from the shaft, only maintenance personnel can reconnect it. That is why disconnection is only commanded when the procedure requires it and with the engine turning. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 31 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Only maintenance personnel","The crew, by pressing the pb again on ground","It reconnects itself when the engine is shut down and restarted","It reconnects automatically if the temperature drops below 180 °C"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-DIST-003","es":{"q":"¿Qué barra NO puede alimentar un solo generador de motor en vuelo?","keys":["bus","entertainment","generador","motor","alimentar","excepto"],"answer":"Un generador de motor puede alimentar toda la red EXCEPTO el DC BUS Entertainment, que necesita dos generadores (salvo en tierra, donde bastan el APU GEN no sobrecargado o la energía externa). Las barras esenciales sí quedan cubiertas por un solo generador. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-10 · p. 11 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["El DC BUS Entertainment","El AC ESS BUS","El DC ESS BUS","El DC BAT BUS"]},"en":{"q":"Which bus can a single engine generator NOT supply in flight?","keys":["bus","entertainment","engine","generator","supply","whole"],"answer":"An engine generator can supply the whole network EXCEPT the DC BUS Entertainment, which needs two generators (except on ground, where the non-overloaded APU GEN or external power suffice). The essential buses are covered by a single generator. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-10 · p. 11 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["The DC BUS Entertainment","The AC ESS BUS","The DC ESS BUS","The DC BAT BUS"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-DCG-003","es":{"q":"¿Para qué sirve el cuarto transformador rectificador, el TR Entertainment?","keys":["alimentar","barra","entertainment","dedicada","sistema","entretenimiento"],"answer":"El TR Entertainment es un cuarto TR dedicado a la barra DC Entertainment, que alimenta el sistema de entretenimiento a bordo (IFE) atendiendo sus necesidades sin cargar los TR principales. El respaldo del circuito DC esencial lo da el ESS TR, no éste. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Para alimentar la barra DC Entertainment dedicada al sistema de entretenimiento a bordo (IFE)","Para alimentar el DC ESS BUS en emergencia","Para cargar las baterías más rápido","Para sustituir al TR 1 o al TR 2 si fallan"]},"en":{"q":"What is the fourth transformer rectifier, the TR Entertainment, used for?","keys":["power","entertainment","bus","dedicated","flight","system"],"answer":"The TR Entertainment is a fourth TR dedicated to the DC Entertainment bus, which powers the In-Flight Entertainment (IFE) system, meeting its needs without loading the main TRs. The backup of the essential DC circuit is provided by the ESS TR, not this one. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["To power the DC Entertainment bus dedicated to the In-Flight Entertainment (IFE) system","To power the DC ESS BUS in emergency","To charge the batteries faster","To replace TR 1 or TR 2 if they fail"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-002","es":{"q":"¿Qué permite hacer el pulsador COMMERCIAL del panel superior?","keys":["conectar","desconectar","golpe","cargas","comerciales","luces"],"answer":"El pulsador COMMERCIAL conecta o desconecta en bloque todas las cargas comerciales del avión: luces de cabina y carga, agua y aseos, protección de hielo del drain mast, galley, entretenimiento de pasaje y carga semiautomática. Es útil, por ejemplo, para aislar cargas ante ciertos olores o humos. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 33 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Conectar o desconectar de golpe todas las cargas comerciales: luces de cabina y carga, agua/aseos, protección de hielo del drain mast, galley, entretenimiento de pasaje y carga semiautomática","Desconectar únicamente los galleys","Aislar las barras esenciales del resto de la red","Conmutar la alimentación del AC ESS entre AC BUS 1 y AC BUS 2"]},"en":{"q":"What does the COMMERCIAL pushbutton on the overhead panel allow?","keys":["switch","commercial","loads","cabin","cargo","lights"],"answer":"The COMMERCIAL pushbutton switches all the aircraft's commercial loads on or off as a block: cabin and cargo lights, water and toilet system, drain-mast ice protection, galley, passenger entertainment and semi-automatic cargo loading. It is useful, for example, to isolate loads in response to certain smells or smoke. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 33 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Switch all commercial loads on or off at once: cabin and cargo lights, water/toilet, drain-mast ice protection, galley, passenger entertainment and semi-automatic cargo loading","Shed only the galleys","Isolate the essential buses from the rest of the network","Switch AC ESS supply between AC BUS 1 and AC BUS 2"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-DCG-004","es":{"q":"¿En qué casos alimenta el ESS TR el circuito DC esencial?","keys":["fallan","generadores","motor","apu","falla","ess"],"answer":"El ESS TR (tercer TR, idéntico) puede alimentar el DC ESS BUS desde el generador de emergencia si fallan todos los generadores de motor y de APU, o bien sustituir a un TR principal cuando falla el TR 1 o el TR 2. Es la garantía del circuito DC esencial. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Cuando fallan todos los generadores de motor y de APU, o cuando falla el TR 1 o el TR 2","Sólo cuando fallan las dos baterías","Únicamente en tierra con energía externa","Sólo cuando el APU está en marcha"]},"en":{"q":"In which cases does the ESS TR supply the essential DC circuit?","keys":["engine","apu","generators","fails","ess","third"],"answer":"The ESS TR (third, identical TR) can power the DC ESS BUS from the emergency generator if all engine and APU generators fail, or replace a main TR when TR 1 or TR 2 fails. It is the guarantee of the essential DC circuit. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 8 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["When all engine and APU generators fail, or when TR 1 or TR 2 fails","Only when both batteries fail","Only on ground with external power","Only when the APU is running"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-EMER-004","es":{"q":"¿Bajo qué condiciones se despliega la RAT automáticamente?","keys":["pierden","bus","velocidad","superior","100","rat"],"answer":"La RAT se despliega automáticamente si se pierden AC BUS 1 y AC BUS 2 y la velocidad supera 100 kt. Presuriza el circuito azul, que acciona el generador de emergencia. Por debajo de 100 kt la RAT no genera suficiente y la red pasa a baterías. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["Cuando se pierden AC BUS 1 y AC BUS 2 y la velocidad es superior a 100 kt","Cuando se pierde un solo AC BUS, a cualquier velocidad","Cuando falla un motor, independientemente de las barras","Cuando la tensión de batería baja de 25 V"]},"en":{"q":"Under what conditions does the RAT extend automatically?","keys":["bus","speed","above","100","rat","extends"],"answer":"The RAT extends automatically if both AC BUS 1 and AC BUS 2 are lost and speed is above 100 kt. It pressurizes the blue circuit, which drives the emergency generator. Below 100 kt the RAT does not produce enough and the network transfers to the batteries. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["When AC BUS 1 and AC BUS 2 are both lost and speed is above 100 kt","When a single AC BUS is lost, at any speed","When an engine fails, regardless of the buses","When battery voltage drops below 25 V"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-EMER-005","es":{"q":"Con el generador de emergencia en marcha, ¿qué barras alimenta y cómo llega la DC?","keys":["ess","bus","directamente","traves","generador","emergencia"],"answer":"El generador de emergencia alimenta el AC ESS BUS y, a través del ESS TR, el DC ESS BUS. No restablece las barras principales (AC BUS 1/2, DC BUS 1/2): sólo la red esencial que permite volar, navegar y comunicar. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["El AC ESS BUS directamente, y el DC ESS BUS a través del ESS TR","El DC ESS BUS directamente, y el AC ESS BUS a través del static inverter","Todas las barras principales AC BUS 1 y 2","Sólo el DC BAT BUS"]},"en":{"q":"With the emergency generator running, which buses does it supply and how is DC provided?","keys":["ess","bus","directly","through","emergency","generator"],"answer":"The emergency generator supplies the AC ESS BUS and, through the ESS TR, the DC ESS BUS. It does not restore the main buses (AC BUS 1/2, DC BUS 1/2): only the essential network that allows to fly, navigate and communicate. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["The AC ESS BUS directly, and the DC ESS BUS through the ESS TR","The DC ESS BUS directly, and the AC ESS BUS through the static inverter","All main buses AC BUS 1 and 2","Only the DC BAT BUS"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-ABN-002","es":{"q":"¿Por qué motivos abre automáticamente el contactor de un TR y qué ocurre entonces?","keys":["sobrecalentamiento","corriente","minima","sustituye","ess","alimenta"],"answer":"El contactor de un TR abre automáticamente por sobrecalentamiento (overheat) o por corriente mínima. El otro TR sustituye al averiado y el ESS TR alimenta el DC ESS BUS. Es una reconfiguración automática, sin desplegar RAT ni conectar baterías. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 18 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Por sobrecalentamiento o corriente mínima; el otro TR lo sustituye y el ESS TR alimenta el DC ESS BUS","Por sobretensión; el ESS TR queda inoperativo","Por baja frecuencia; se conectan las baterías","Por sobrecarga del generador; se despliega la RAT"]},"en":{"q":"For what reasons does a TR contactor open automatically and what happens then?","keys":["overheat","minimum","current","other","replaces","ess"],"answer":"A TR contactor opens automatically due to overheat or minimum current. The other TR replaces the faulty one and the ESS TR supplies the DC ESS BUS. It is an automatic reconfiguration, without RAT deployment or battery connection. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 18 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Due to overheat or minimum current; the other TR replaces it and the ESS TR supplies the DC ESS BUS","Due to overvoltage; the ESS TR becomes inoperative","Due to low frequency; the batteries connect","Due to generator overload; the RAT deploys"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-003","es":{"q":"¿Qué hace el AC ESS FEED pb en posición normal y qué aporta el AC ESS FEED Auto Switching?","keys":["normal","alimenta","ess","bus","switching","automaticamente"],"answer":"En posición normal el AC ESS BUS se alimenta del AC BUS 1. Con el AC ESS FEED Auto Switching, si se pierde el AC BUS 1 el AC BUS 2 pasa a alimentar el AC ESS automáticamente (y el ESS TR el DC ESS), sin acción del piloto. Seleccionar ALTN lo fuerza al AC BUS 2. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 32 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["En normal alimenta el AC ESS desde el AC BUS 1; con auto switching el AC BUS 2 lo alimenta automáticamente si se pierde el AC BUS 1","En normal alimenta el AC ESS desde el AC BUS 2; el auto switching lo pasa al AC BUS 1","En normal conecta el static inverter; el auto switching conecta el generador de emergencia","En normal desconecta el AC ESS; el auto switching lo reconecta al perder ambos AC BUS"]},"en":{"q":"What does the AC ESS FEED pb do in normal position and what does AC ESS FEED Auto Switching add?","keys":["normal","feeds","ess","bus","switching","automatically"],"answer":"In normal position the AC ESS BUS is fed from AC BUS 1. With AC ESS FEED Auto Switching, if AC BUS 1 is lost AC BUS 2 automatically feeds the AC ESS (and the ESS TR the DC ESS), with no pilot action. Selecting ALTN forces it to AC BUS 2. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 32 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Normal feeds AC ESS from AC BUS 1; with auto switching AC BUS 2 feeds it automatically if AC BUS 1 is lost","Normal feeds AC ESS from AC BUS 2; auto switching transfers it to AC BUS 1","Normal connects the static inverter; auto switching connects the emergency generator","Normal disconnects AC ESS; auto switching reconnects it on loss of both AC BUS"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-004","es":{"q":"¿En qué situaciones están cerrados AMBOS bus tie contactors (BTC)?","keys":["operacion","monomotor","alimentando","generador","apu","energia"],"answer":"Los dos BTC se cierran cuando una sola fuente debe alimentar ambos AC BUS: operación monomotor, alimentación por el generador de APU o por energía externa. Con los dos generadores de motor en marcha, cada uno alimenta su barra y los BTC están abiertos. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 32 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["En operación monomotor, o alimentando con el generador de APU, o con energía externa","Siempre que los dos motores estén en marcha","Nunca; sólo puede haber uno cerrado","Sólo con el generador de emergencia en marcha"]},"en":{"q":"In which situations are BOTH bus tie contactors (BTC) closed?","keys":["single","engine","operation","supplying","apu","generator"],"answer":"Both BTCs close when a single source must feed both AC BUSes: single-engine operation, supply by the APU generator or by external power. With both engine generators running, each feeds its own bus and the BTCs are open. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 32 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["In single-engine operation, or supplying with the APU generator, or with external power","Whenever both engines are running","Never; only one can be closed","Only with the emergency generator running"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-005","es":{"q":"El RAT MAN ON pb en posición AUTO, ¿bajo qué condiciones extiende la RAT y acciona el generador de emergencia?","keys":["bus","alimentados","velocidad","superior","100","logica"],"answer":"En AUTO, la lógica extiende la RAT y acciona el generador de emergencia cuando AC BUS 1 y AC BUS 2 no están alimentados y la velocidad supera 100 kt. Pulsando el pb se selecciona extensión manual de la RAT (acoplamiento del gen de emergencia 3 s después). (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 35 · rev 21 MAR 17)","opts":["Con AC BUS 1 y AC BUS 2 no alimentados y velocidad superior a 100 kt","Con perder un solo AC BUS a cualquier velocidad","Con velocidad inferior a 100 kt y ambos AC BUS perdidos","Con fallo de un motor"]},"en":{"q":"With the RAT MAN ON pb in AUTO, under what conditions does the RAT extend and drive the emergency generator?","keys":["bus","unpowered","speed","above","100","logic"],"answer":"In AUTO, the logic extends the RAT and drives the emergency generator when AC BUS 1 and AC BUS 2 are unpowered and speed is above 100 kt. Pressing the pb selects manual RAT extension (emergency generator coupling 3 s later). (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 35 · rev 21 MAR 17)","opts":["With AC BUS 1 and AC BUS 2 unpowered and speed above 100 kt","On losing a single AC BUS at any speed","With speed below 100 kt and both AC BUS lost","On failure of one engine"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-006","es":{"q":"¿Cuándo se enciende en rojo la luz FAULT del panel EMER ELEC PWR?","keys":["generador","emergencia","alimenta","bus","estan","alimentados"],"answer":"La luz FAULT (roja) se enciende si el generador de emergencia NO está alimentando cuando AC BUS 1 y AC BUS 2 no están alimentados: indica que la red esencial no tiene su fuente prevista. No es una simple indicación de RAT desplegada. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 35 · rev 21 MAR 17)","opts":["Cuando el generador de emergencia no alimenta y AC BUS 1 y 2 no están alimentados","Siempre que la RAT esté desplegada","Cuando el APU GEN falla","Cuando la carga del generador de emergencia supera el 100 %"]},"en":{"q":"When does the FAULT light on the EMER ELEC PWR panel come on red?","keys":["emergency","generator","supplying","bus","unpowered","fault"],"answer":"The (red) FAULT light comes on if the emergency generator is NOT supplying while AC BUS 1 and AC BUS 2 are unpowered: it indicates the essential network lacks its intended source. It is not a mere RAT-deployed indication. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 35 · rev 21 MAR 17)","opts":["When the emergency generator is not supplying and AC BUS 1 and 2 are unpowered","Whenever the RAT is deployed","When the APU GEN fails","When the emergency generator load exceeds 100 %"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-007","es":{"q":"¿En qué condiciones se desconectan automáticamente los galleys principales?","keys":["vuelo","funciona","generador","tierra","alimenta","motor"],"answer":"Los galleys principales se desconectan automáticamente en vuelo cuando sólo funciona un generador, y en tierra cuando alimenta un único generador de motor (con APU GEN o EXT PWR sí hay galleys). La luz FAULT del GALLEY se enciende si la carga de cualquier generador supera el 100 %. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 33 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["En vuelo cuando sólo funciona un generador; en tierra cuando alimenta un solo generador de motor","Siempre que el APU esté en marcha","Sólo con el generador de emergencia en marcha","Cuando la tensión de batería baja de 26,5 V"]},"en":{"q":"Under what conditions are the main galleys shed automatically?","keys":["flight","generator","operates","ground","supplied","single"],"answer":"The main galleys are shed automatically in flight when only one generator operates, and on ground when supplied by a single engine generator (with APU GEN or EXT PWR galleys are available). The GALLEY FAULT light comes on if any generator's load exceeds 100 %. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 33 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["In flight when only one generator operates; on ground when supplied by a single engine generator","Whenever the APU is running","Only with the emergency generator running","When battery voltage drops below 26.5 V"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-FCTM-001","es":{"q":"En configuración eléctrica de emergencia, según el FCTM, ¿por qué el piloto del asiento izquierdo pasa a ser PF?","keys":["porque","queda","disponible","emer","config","izquierdo"],"answer":"En ELEC EMER CONFIG sólo queda disponible el PFD1 (lado izquierdo), por eso el piloto del asiento izquierdo asume el rol de PF. AP/FD y A/THR se pierden: el vuelo se hace a mano en alternate law y, con el tren abajo, en direct law. (FCTM PR-AEP-ELEC · p. 427 · rev 04 JUN 19)","opts":["Porque sólo queda disponible el PFD1","Porque el sidestick derecho queda inhibido","Por reparto estándar de tareas en emergencia","Porque el AP sólo se engancha desde la izquierda"]},"en":{"q":"In emergency electrical configuration, per the FCTM, why does the left-seat pilot become PF?","keys":["because","remains","available","emer","config","pilot"],"answer":"In ELEC EMER CONFIG only PFD1 (left side) remains available, so the left-seat pilot takes the PF role. AP/FD and A/THR are lost: the flight is flown manually in alternate law and, with gear down, in direct law. (FCTM PR-AEP-ELEC · p. 427 · rev 04 JUN 19)","opts":["Because only PFD1 remains available","Because the right sidestick is inhibited","By standard emergency task-sharing","Because the AP can only be engaged from the left"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-FCTM-002","es":{"q":"Volando en configuración eléctrica de emergencia, ¿qué ocurre con la ley de mando al bajar el tren de aterrizaje?","keys":["revierte","direct","emer","config","avion","vuela"],"answer":"En ELEC EMER CONFIG el avión vuela en alternate law y, al bajar el tren, la ley revierte a direct law. El piloto debe anticipar una respuesta más directa en cabeceo y ausencia de protecciones en la toma. (FCTM PR-AEP-ELEC · p. 427 · rev 16 MAY 23)","opts":["La ley revierte a direct law","La ley pasa a normal law","No cambia: permanece en alternate law","Se activa la protección de alto ángulo de ataque"]},"en":{"q":"Flying in emergency electrical configuration, what happens to the control law when the landing gear is lowered?","keys":["reverts","direct","emer","config","aircraft","flies"],"answer":"In ELEC EMER CONFIG the aircraft flies in alternate law and, on lowering the gear, the law reverts to direct law. The pilot must anticipate a more direct pitch response and no protections in the flare. (FCTM PR-AEP-ELEC · p. 427 · rev 16 MAY 23)","opts":["The law reverts to direct law","The law changes to normal law","It does not change: it stays in alternate law","High angle-of-attack protection activates"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-FCTM-003","es":{"q":"El FCTM indica que en configuración eléctrica de emergencia el ECAM muestra LAND ASAP en rojo. ¿Cómo debe interpretarse?","keys":["emergencia","seria","mayday","vuelo","prolongado","recomendable"],"answer":"El FCTM matiza el LAND ASAP rojo: es una emergencia seria que se declara MAYDAY y en la que el vuelo prolongado no es recomendable, pero sería imprudente intentar aproximación a un campo mal equipado con tiempo marginal. Se busca el mejor compromiso, no el más cercano a ciegas. (FCTM PR-AEP-ELEC · p. 427 · rev 04 JUN 19)","opts":["Es una emergencia seria (MAYDAY) y el vuelo prolongado no es recomendable, pero no obliga a aterrizar en un campo mal equipado con tiempo marginal","Aterrizar en el aeropuerto más cercano sea cual sea su equipamiento o el tiempo","Puede ignorarse porque el generador de emergencia cubre todo","Sólo aplica si además fallan las baterías"]},"en":{"q":"The FCTM states that in emergency electrical configuration the ECAM shows LAND ASAP in red. How should it be interpreted?","keys":["serious","emergency","mayday","prolonged","flight","recommended"],"answer":"The FCTM qualifies the red LAND ASAP: it is a serious emergency, declared MAYDAY, in which prolonged flight is not recommended, yet it would be unwise to attempt an approach at a poorly equipped field in marginal weather. Seek the best compromise, not the nearest one blindly. (FCTM PR-AEP-ELEC · p. 427 · rev 04 JUN 19)","opts":["It is a serious emergency (MAYDAY) and prolonged flight is not recommended, but it does not force a landing at a poorly equipped field in marginal weather","Land at the nearest airport regardless of its equipment or the weather","It can be ignored because the emergency generator covers everything","It only applies if the batteries also fail"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-IND-003","es":{"q":"En la página ELEC, ¿fuera de qué márgenes se vuelven ámbar la tensión y la frecuencia del generador de emergencia?","keys":["tension","110","120","frecuencia","390","410"],"answer":"La tensión del generador de emergencia se vuelve ámbar por debajo de 110 V o por encima de 120 V, y la frecuencia por debajo de 390 Hz o por encima de 410 Hz. Los mismos márgenes AC aplican a GEN, APU GEN y EXT PWR. Ojo: 25/31 V son márgenes DC (batería/TR). (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 43 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Tensión < 110 V o > 120 V; frecuencia < 390 Hz o > 410 Hz","Tensión < 100 V o > 130 V; frecuencia < 380 Hz o > 420 Hz","Tensión < 115 V o > 200 V; frecuencia fija 400 Hz","Tensión < 25 V o > 31 V; frecuencia < 390 Hz o > 410 Hz"]},"en":{"q":"On the ELEC page, outside which limits do the emergency generator voltage and frequency become amber?","keys":["voltage","110","120","frequency","390","410"],"answer":"The emergency generator voltage becomes amber below 110 V or above 120 V, and the frequency below 390 Hz or above 410 Hz. The same AC limits apply to GEN, APU GEN and EXT PWR. Note: 25/31 V are DC limits (battery/TR). (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 43 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Voltage < 110 V or > 120 V; frequency < 390 Hz or > 410 Hz","Voltage < 100 V or > 130 V; frequency < 380 Hz or > 420 Hz","Voltage < 115 V or > 200 V; fixed 400 Hz frequency","Voltage < 25 V or > 31 V; frequency < 390 Hz or > 410 Hz"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-ABN-003","es":{"q":"Si se pierden a la vez el TR 1 y el TR 2, ¿qué barras DC quedan afectadas y cuál se conserva?","keys":["pierden","bus","bat","ess","alimenta","perdidos"],"answer":"Con TR 1 y TR 2 perdidos se pierden DC BUS 1, DC BUS 2 y DC BAT BUS, pero el DC ESS BUS lo sigue alimentando el ESS TR. Es la clave de la arquitectura: el circuito esencial tiene su propio TR de respaldo. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 19 · rev 04 JUN 19)","opts":["Se pierden DC BUS 1, DC BUS 2 y DC BAT BUS; el DC ESS BUS lo alimenta el ESS TR","Se pierde todo el sistema DC, incluido el DC ESS BUS","Se conservan DC BUS 1 y DC BUS 2; se pierde el DC ESS BUS","Sólo se pierde el DC BAT BUS"]},"en":{"q":"If TR 1 and TR 2 are lost simultaneously, which DC buses are affected and which one is preserved?","keys":["bus","bat","ess","supplied","still","architecture"],"answer":"With TR 1 and TR 2 lost, DC BUS 1, DC BUS 2 and DC BAT BUS are lost, but the DC ESS BUS is still supplied by the ESS TR. That is the key of the architecture: the essential circuit has its own backup TR. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 19 · rev 04 JUN 19)","opts":["DC BUS 1, DC BUS 2 and DC BAT BUS are lost; the DC ESS BUS is supplied by the ESS TR","The whole DC system is lost, including the DC ESS BUS","DC BUS 1 and DC BUS 2 are preserved; the DC ESS BUS is lost","Only the DC BAT BUS is lost"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-EMER-006","es":{"q":"En configuración de emergencia con el avión en tierra, ¿qué sucede al bajar de 50 kt?","keys":["desconecta","ess","bus","consiguiente","perdida","display"],"answer":"En tierra, por debajo de 100 kt el DC BAT BUS se conecta a las baterías y por debajo de 50 kt se desconecta el AC ESS BUS, lo que provoca la pérdida de todas las display units. El FCTM avisa: aproximándose a 50 kt en el rodaje de aterrizaje se pierden todas las pantallas. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["Se desconecta (shed) el AC ESS BUS, con la consiguiente pérdida de todas las display units","Se conecta el DC BAT BUS a las baterías por primera vez","Arranca el APU automáticamente","Se despliega la RAT de nuevo"]},"en":{"q":"In emergency configuration with the aircraft on ground, what happens below 50 kt?","keys":["ess","bus","display","units","ground","below"],"answer":"On ground, below 100 kt the DC BAT BUS connects to the batteries and below 50 kt the AC ESS BUS is shed, causing the loss of all display units. The FCTM warns: approaching 50 kt in the landing roll all display units are lost. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["The AC ESS BUS is shed, with the loss of all display units","The DC BAT BUS connects to the batteries for the first time","The APU starts automatically","The RAT deploys again"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-008","es":{"q":"Con AC BUS 1 y 2 no energizados y sin generador de emergencia, ¿qué alimenta cada batería?","keys":["bat","alimenta","stat","inv","bus","velocidad"],"answer":"Con ambos AC BUS caídos y sin generador de emergencia, la BAT 1 alimenta el AC STAT INV BUS (static inverter) y, por encima de 50 kt, el AC ESS BUS; la BAT 2 alimenta el DC ESS BUS. Es el reparto que sostiene la red mínima con sólo baterías. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 30 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["La BAT 1 alimenta el AC STAT INV BUS y, si la velocidad supera 50 kt, el AC ESS BUS; la BAT 2 alimenta el DC ESS BUS","La BAT 1 alimenta el DC ESS BUS y la BAT 2 el AC ESS BUS","Ambas baterías alimentan por igual todas las barras esenciales","La BAT 2 alimenta el AC STAT INV BUS y la BAT 1 el DC BAT BUS"]},"en":{"q":"With AC BUS 1 and 2 unpowered and no emergency generator, what does each battery supply?","keys":["bat","supplies","stat","inv","bus","speed"],"answer":"With both AC BUS down and no emergency generator, BAT 1 supplies the AC STAT INV BUS (static inverter) and, above 50 kt, the AC ESS BUS; BAT 2 supplies the DC ESS BUS. This is the split that sustains the minimum network on batteries only. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 30 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["BAT 1 supplies the AC STAT INV BUS and, if speed is above 50 kt, the AC ESS BUS; BAT 2 supplies the DC ESS BUS","BAT 1 supplies the DC ESS BUS and BAT 2 the AC ESS BUS","Both batteries equally supply all essential buses","BAT 2 supplies the AC STAT INV BUS and BAT 1 the DC BAT BUS"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-IND-004","es":{"q":"En la página ELEC, ¿qué condiciones hacen ámbar la indicación de tensión de batería y cuándo la corriente de descarga es relevante?","keys":["tension","25","31","corriente","descarga","encima"],"answer":"La tensión de batería se muestra ámbar por debajo de 25 V o por encima de 31 V, y la corriente de descarga es relevante (ámbar) por encima de 5 A. No confundir con los 26,5 V (umbral de inicio de carga) ni con los 110/120 V, que son márgenes AC. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 40 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Tensión < 25 V o > 31 V; corriente de descarga por encima de 5 A","Tensión < 26,5 V; descarga > 1 A","Tensión < 110 V o > 120 V; descarga > 4 A","Tensión < 24 V; descarga > 10 A"]},"en":{"q":"On the ELEC page, what conditions turn the battery voltage indication amber and when is the discharge current relevant?","keys":["voltage","25","31","discharge","current","above"],"answer":"Battery voltage shows amber below 25 V or above 31 V, and discharge current is relevant (amber) above 5 A. Do not confuse with 26.5 V (charge-start threshold) nor with 110/120 V, which are AC limits. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 40 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Voltage < 25 V or > 31 V; discharge current above 5 A","Voltage < 26.5 V; discharge > 1 A","Voltage < 110 V or > 120 V; discharge > 4 A","Voltage < 24 V; discharge > 10 A"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-ABN-004","es":{"q":"Ante el fallo del AC BUS 1, ¿cómo se restablece la alimentación del DC BUS 1 y del DC BAT BUS?","keys":["bus","alimenta","bat","automaticamente","perdido","ess"],"answer":"Con el AC BUS 1 perdido, el AC ESS pasa al AC BUS 2 (auto switching) y, en el lado DC, el DC BUS 2 alimenta el DC BUS 1 y el DC BAT BUS automáticamente tras 5 s. El retardo de 5 s es un detalle que suele preguntarse. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 17 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["El DC BUS 2 alimenta el DC BUS 1 y el DC BAT BUS automáticamente tras 5 s","Inmediatamente por el ESS TR","Por las baterías, mientras la velocidad supere 100 kt","No se restablecen: quedan perdidos hasta recuperar el AC BUS 1"]},"en":{"q":"On failure of AC BUS 1, how is DC BUS 1 and DC BAT BUS supply restored?","keys":["bus","supplies","bat","automatically","after","ess"],"answer":"With AC BUS 1 lost, the AC ESS transfers to AC BUS 2 (auto switching) and, on the DC side, DC BUS 2 supplies DC BUS 1 and DC BAT BUS automatically after 5 s. The 5 s delay is a detail often asked. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 17 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["DC BUS 2 supplies DC BUS 1 and DC BAT BUS automatically after 5 s","Immediately by the ESS TR","By the batteries, while speed is above 100 kt","They are not restored: they stay lost until AC BUS 1 recovers"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-EMER-007","es":{"q":"Cuando la RAT entra en pérdida (stall) y el generador de emergencia deja de alimentar, ¿qué ocurre con la red de emergencia?","keys":["transfiere","automaticamente","baterias","static","inverter","desconectan"],"answer":"Al entrar la RAT en pérdida, el circuito azul deja de presurizarse y el generador de emergencia deja de alimentar. La red se transfiere automáticamente a las baterías y al static inverter, y se desconectan las barras AC SHED ESS y DC SHED ESS para aligerar consumo. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["Se transfiere automáticamente a baterías y static inverter, y se desconectan (shed) el AC SHED ESS y el DC SHED ESS","Se pierde por completo hasta rearmar la RAT manualmente","El APU asume automáticamente toda la red","El ESS TR pasa a alimentarse directamente del AC BUS 1"]},"en":{"q":"When the RAT stalls and the emergency generator stops supplying, what happens to the emergency network?","keys":["transfers","automatically","batteries","static","inverter","ess"],"answer":"When the RAT stalls, the blue circuit is no longer pressurized and the emergency generator stops supplying. The network automatically transfers to the batteries and static inverter, and the AC SHED ESS and DC SHED ESS buses are shed to reduce consumption. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["It transfers automatically to batteries and static inverter, and the AC SHED ESS and DC SHED ESS are shed","It is completely lost until the RAT is manually rearmed","The APU automatically takes over the whole network","The ESS TR is fed directly from AC BUS 1"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-009","es":{"q":"Respecto a la carga de baterías: ¿a qué tensión se inicia la carga, cuándo termina el ciclo y qué retardo hay en vuelo?","keys":["empieza","26","termina","corriente","carga","vuelo"],"answer":"La batería se conecta para cargar cuando su tensión cae por debajo de 26,5 V; el ciclo termina cuando la corriente de carga baja de 4 A. En tierra la conexión es inmediata; en vuelo se aplica un retardo de 30 min. No confundir con los 25/31 V de la indicación ámbar. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 30 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Empieza < 26,5 V, termina cuando la corriente de carga baja de 4 A; en vuelo con 30 min de retardo (en tierra inmediato)","Empieza < 24 V, termina con corriente < 1 A, sin retardo","Empieza < 31 V, termina con corriente < 5 A, retardo de 5 min en vuelo","Empieza < 25 V, termina cuando la tensión alcanza 31 V, retardo de 3 min"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding battery charging: at what voltage does charging start, when does the cycle end and what delay applies in flight?","keys":["starts","26","charge","current","drops","below"],"answer":"The battery connects to charge when its voltage drops below 26.5 V; the cycle ends when charge current drops below 4 A. On ground the connection is immediate; in flight a 30 min delay applies. Do not confuse with the 25/31 V amber-indication limits. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 30 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Starts < 26.5 V, ends when charge current drops below 4 A; in flight after a 30 min delay (immediate on ground)","Starts < 24 V, ends when current < 1 A, no delay","Starts < 31 V, ends when current < 5 A, 5 min delay in flight","Starts < 25 V, ends when voltage reaches 31 V, 3 min delay"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-010","es":{"q":"¿Qué provoca el encendido de la luz FAULT del IDG y qué salvedad hay a bajo régimen de motor?","keys":["sobrecalentamiento","aceite","salida","180","presion","inhibida"],"answer":"La luz FAULT del IDG se enciende por sobrecalentamiento del aceite de salida (> 180 °C) o por baja presión de aceite, esta última inhibida a bajo régimen (N2 por debajo del 14 %). Los 147 °C son sólo un aviso (advisory) con pulso, no la FAULT. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 31 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Sobrecalentamiento del aceite de salida (> 180 °C) o baja presión de aceite; la baja presión está inhibida con N2 por debajo del 14 %","Sólo la baja presión de aceite, sin ninguna inhibición","Sobrecarga del generador por encima del 100 %","Cualquier temperatura por encima de 147 °C"]},"en":{"q":"What causes the IDG FAULT light to come on and what caveat applies at low engine speed?","keys":["overheat","outlet","180","pressure","inhibited","below"],"answer":"The IDG FAULT light comes on due to outlet-oil overheat (> 180 °C) or low oil pressure, the latter inhibited at low engine speed (N2 below 14 %). The 147 °C is only a pulsing advisory, not the FAULT. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 31 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Overheat of the outlet oil (> 180 °C) or low oil pressure; low pressure is inhibited with N2 below 14 %","Only low oil pressure, with no inhibition","Generator overload above 100 %","Any temperature above 147 °C"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-011","es":{"q":"Además de la desconexión manual, ¿existe alguna desconexión automática del IDG?","keys":["desconexion","termica","automatica","temperatura","alcanza","200"],"answer":"Sí: se produce una desconexión térmica automática del IDG si la temperatura alcanza 200 °C. A 180 °C se enciende la FAULT (sobrecalentamiento), pero la desconexión automática por temperatura es a 200 °C. También cuenta la salvedad de mantener el pb más de 3 s (daña el mecanismo). (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 31 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Sí: una desconexión térmica automática si la temperatura alcanza 200 °C","No: el IDG sólo se desconecta con el pb","Sí, automática si la presión de aceite baja de un umbral","Sí, automática por sobrecarga eléctrica del generador"]},"en":{"q":"Besides manual disconnection, is there any automatic IDG disconnection?","keys":["automatic","thermal","disconnection","temperature","reaches","200"],"answer":"Yes: an automatic thermal disconnection of the IDG occurs if the temperature reaches 200 °C. At 180 °C the FAULT comes on (overheat), but automatic temperature disconnection is at 200 °C. Also note holding the pb for more than 3 s damages the mechanism. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 31 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Yes: an automatic thermal disconnection if the temperature reaches 200 °C","No: the IDG only disconnects with the pb","Yes, automatic if oil pressure drops below a threshold","Yes, automatic due to generator electrical overload"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-012","es":{"q":"Tras una FAULT de generador, ¿qué limitación tiene el rearme (reset) si el fallo fue un fallo diferencial?","keys":["fallo","diferencial","dispara","proteccion","reset","tiene"],"answer":"Si la protección se disparó por un fallo diferencial, el reset del GEN pb no tiene efecto después de dos intentos. Insistir no restablece el generador: la protección bloquea para evitar reconectar una avería real. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 31 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Si un fallo diferencial dispara la protección, el reset no tiene efecto después de dos intentos","El reset no tiene límite: puede intentarse indefinidamente","El reset sólo puede hacerse en tierra","El reset requiere desconectar antes el IDG"]},"en":{"q":"After a generator FAULT, what limitation applies to the reset if the failure was a differential fault?","keys":["differential","fault","trips","protection","reset","effect"],"answer":"If the protection tripped due to a differential fault, resetting the GEN pb has no effect after two attempts. Insisting does not restore the generator: the protection latches to avoid reconnecting a real fault. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 31 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["If a differential fault trips the protection, reset has no effect after two attempts","Reset has no limit: it can be attempted indefinitely","Reset can only be done on ground","Reset requires disconnecting the IDG first"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-SMOKE-001","es":{"q":"En la configuración de humo (smoke) del sistema eléctrico, ¿qué la diferencia de la configuración de emergencia normal y cuánto equipo desconecta?","keys":["distribucion","igual","emergencia","salvo","bombas","combustible"],"answer":"En smoke config las barras principales se desconectan y la distribución es la de la configuración eléctrica de emergencia, salvo que las bombas de combustible se conectan aguas arriba del GEN 1 line connector. El procedimiento desconecta aproximadamente el 75 % del equipo; lo que queda se alimenta por los C/B del overhead. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 25 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Distribución igual a la de emergencia salvo que las bombas de combustible se conectan aguas arriba del GEN 1 line connector; desconecta ~75 % del equipo","Es idéntica en todo; desconecta el 25 % del equipo","Mantiene todas las barras principales; no desconecta equipo","Alimenta todo desde las baterías; desconecta el 50 %"]},"en":{"q":"In the electrical smoke configuration, what makes it different from the standard emergency configuration and how much equipment does it shed?","keys":["distribution","emergency","except","pumps","connected","upstream"],"answer":"In smoke config the main buses are shed and the distribution matches the electrical emergency configuration, except the fuel pumps are connected upstream of the GEN 1 line connector. The procedure sheds about 75 % of equipment; what remains is fed through the overhead C/Bs. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 25 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Same distribution as emergency except the fuel pumps are connected upstream of the GEN 1 line connector; sheds ~75 % of equipment","Identical in everything; sheds 25 % of equipment","Keeps all main buses; sheds no equipment","Feeds everything from the batteries; sheds 50 %"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-FCTM-004","es":{"q":"Según el FCTM, en configuración eléctrica de emergencia, ¿qué consecuencias tiene la pérdida de los BSCU sobre frenado y reversas?","keys":["pierden","nws","frenado","alternativo","modulacion","presion"],"answer":"Con los BSCU perdidos se van la dirección de morro (NWS) y el anti-skid; se frena con frenado alternativo modulando la presión amarilla hasta 1 000 PSI, y las reversas no están disponibles. Hay que planificar la desaceleración con esos condicionantes. (FCTM PR-AEP-ELEC · p. 427 · rev 16 MAY 23)","opts":["Se pierden NWS y anti-skid; se usa frenado alternativo con modulación de presión amarilla hasta 1 000 PSI; las reversas no están disponibles","Sólo se pierde el anti-skid; las reversas funcionan con normalidad","No hay efecto sobre el frenado; sólo se pierde el autobrake","Se pierde todo el frenado; hay que usar el freno de aparcamiento para detener el avión"]},"en":{"q":"Per the FCTM, in emergency electrical configuration, what are the consequences of losing the BSCU on braking and reversers?","keys":["nws","alternate","braking","yellow","pressure","modulation"],"answer":"With the BSCU lost, nose-wheel steering (NWS) and anti-skid are gone; braking is by alternate braking modulating yellow pressure up to 1 000 PSI, and reversers are not available. Deceleration must be planned with those constraints. (FCTM PR-AEP-ELEC · p. 427 · rev 16 MAY 23)","opts":["NWS and anti-skid are lost; alternate braking with yellow pressure modulation up to 1 000 PSI is used; reversers are not available","Only anti-skid is lost; reversers work normally","No effect on braking; only autobrake is lost","All braking is lost; the parking brake must be used to stop the aircraft"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-FCTM-005","es":{"q":"Según el FCTM, ¿qué velocidad mínima de aproximación debe respetarse en configuración eléctrica de emergencia y por qué?","keys":["velocidad","minima","rat","140","mantener","generador"],"answer":"La aproximación debe volarse a la velocidad mínima de RAT (140 kt) como mínimo, para que la RAT siga presurizando el circuito azul y el generador de emergencia mantenga alimentada la red eléctrica esencial. No confundir los 140 kt (mantener alimentación) con los 100 kt (despliegue automático). (FCTM PR-AEP-ELEC · p. 427 · rev 16 MAY 23)","opts":["Al menos la velocidad mínima de RAT (140 kt), para mantener el generador de emergencia alimentando la red","100 kt, que es la velocidad a la que se despliega la RAT","VLS, para tener margen de maniobra","160 kt, para compensar la direct law"]},"en":{"q":"Per the FCTM, what minimum approach speed must be respected in emergency electrical configuration and why?","keys":["least","minimum","rat","speed","140","emergency"],"answer":"The approach must be flown at least at the minimum RAT speed (140 kt), so the RAT keeps pressurizing the blue circuit and the emergency generator keeps the essential network powered. Do not confuse 140 kt (keep supply) with 100 kt (automatic deployment). (FCTM PR-AEP-ELEC · p. 427 · rev 16 MAY 23)","opts":["At least the minimum RAT speed (140 kt), to keep the emergency generator supplying the network","100 kt, the speed at which the RAT deploys","VLS, to have manoeuvre margin","160 kt, to compensate for direct law"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-013","es":{"q":"Con AC BUS 1 y 2 perdidos por debajo de 100 kt y sin generador de emergencia alimentando, ¿qué hace el sistema con las baterías?","keys":["conecta","baterias","bat","bus","sostener","perdida"],"answer":"La pérdida de AC BUS 1 y 2 por debajo de 100 kt, con el EMER GEN no alimentando, es uno de los casos en que las baterías se conectan al DC BAT BUS. Así se sostiene la red esencial durante la transición hasta que el gen de emergencia alimente o se recupere la red. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 30 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Conecta las baterías al DC BAT BUS para sostener la red","Desconecta las baterías para protegerlas","Arranca el APU automáticamente","Reconecta el AC BUS 1 desde las baterías"]},"en":{"q":"With AC BUS 1 and 2 lost below 100 kt and no emergency generator supplying, what does the system do with the batteries?","keys":["connects","batteries","bat","bus","sustain","network"],"answer":"Loss of AC BUS 1 and 2 below 100 kt, with the EMER GEN not supplying, is one of the cases in which the batteries are connected to the DC BAT BUS. This sustains the essential network during the transition until the emergency generator supplies or the network recovers. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 30 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["It connects the batteries to the DC BAT BUS to sustain the network","It disconnects the batteries to protect them","It starts the APU automatically","It reconnects AC BUS 1 from the batteries"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-SINV-002","es":{"q":"¿Cómo cambia la lógica de activación del static inverter por encima y por debajo de 50 kt cuando sólo las baterías alimentan el avión?","keys":["encima","50","activa","automaticamente","independencia","posicion"],"answer":"Con sólo baterías alimentando: por encima de 50 kt el static inverter se activa automáticamente sea cual sea la posición de los BAT pb; por debajo de 50 kt sólo se activa si ambos BAT pb están en ON. El matiz de los BAT pb a baja velocidad es un detalle de nivel examen. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 20 MAY 19)","opts":["Por encima de 50 kt se activa automáticamente con independencia de la posición de los BAT pb; por debajo de 50 kt sólo si ambos BAT pb están en ON","Siempre requiere ambos BAT pb en ON, con independencia de la velocidad","Por debajo de 50 kt se activa siempre; por encima requiere ambos BAT pb en ON","Sólo se activa con el generador de emergencia en marcha"]},"en":{"q":"How does the static inverter activation logic change above and below 50 kt when only the batteries supply the aircraft?","keys":["above","50","activates","automatically","regardless","bat"],"answer":"With batteries only supplying: above 50 kt the static inverter activates automatically regardless of BAT pb position; below 50 kt it activates only if both BAT pb are ON. The BAT-pb caveat at low speed is an exam-level detail. (FCOM DSC-24-10-20 · p. 7 · rev 20 MAY 19)","opts":["Above 50 kt it activates automatically regardless of BAT pb position; below 50 kt only if both BAT pb are ON","It always requires both BAT pb ON, regardless of speed","Below 50 kt it always activates; above it requires both BAT pb ON","It only activates with the emergency generator running"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-014","es":{"q":"Durante un arranque de APU, ¿qué limitación temporal se aplica a la conexión de las baterías si el generador de emergencia está en marcha?","keys":["conexion","limita","generador","emergencia","marcha","baterias"],"answer":"Las baterías se conectan al DC BAT BUS para el arranque del APU (MASTER SW ON y N < 95 %), pero si el generador de emergencia está en marcha esa conexión se limita a 3 min, para no descargar en exceso las baterías que sostienen la red de emergencia. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 30 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["La conexión se limita a 3 min cuando el generador de emergencia está en marcha","No hay límite: las baterías siguen conectadas todo el arranque","5 min","30 min, igual que el retardo de carga en vuelo"]},"en":{"q":"During an APU start, what time limit applies to the battery connection if the emergency generator is running?","keys":["connection","limited","emergency","generator","running","batteries"],"answer":"The batteries connect to the DC BAT BUS for the APU start (MASTER SW ON and N < 95 %), but if the emergency generator is running that connection is limited to 3 min, to avoid over-draining the batteries sustaining the emergency network. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 30 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["The connection is limited to 3 min when the emergency generator is running","No limit: the batteries stay connected for the whole start","5 min","30 min, same as the in-flight charge delay"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-EMER-008","es":{"q":"En tierra, con sólo las baterías alimentando la red de emergencia, ¿cuándo está disponible el arranque del APU?","keys":["velocidad","inferior","100","tierra","baterias","alimentan"],"answer":"En tierra, si sólo las baterías alimentan la red de emergencia, el arranque del APU está disponible únicamente cuando la velocidad es inferior a 100 kt. Por encima, la carga del arranque no es compatible con la red mínima que sostienen las baterías. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["Sólo cuando la velocidad es inferior a 100 kt","En cualquier momento, a cualquier velocidad","Sólo por encima de 100 kt","Nunca: el APU no puede arrancarse con baterías"]},"en":{"q":"On ground, with only the batteries supplying the emergency network, when is APU start available?","keys":["speed","below","100","ground","batteries","power"],"answer":"On ground, if only the batteries power the emergency network, APU start is available only when speed is below 100 kt. Above that, the start load is not compatible with the minimum network the batteries sustain. (FCOM DSC-24-10-30-30 · p. 20 · rev 09 MAY 23)","opts":["Only when speed is below 100 kt","At any time, at any speed","Only above 100 kt","Never: the APU cannot be started on batteries"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-ELEC-CTL-015","es":{"q":"La lógica de corte automático de baterías en tierra (parking) evita que se descarguen del todo. ¿Bajo qué condiciones abren los contactores y cómo se rearman?","keys":["abren","tierra","bat","fuente","principal","gen"],"answer":"Los contactores automáticos abren cuando: el avión está en tierra, los BAT pb en AUTO, se ha cortado la fuente principal (EXT PWR + GEN) y la tensión de batería es baja. Así se evita descargar las baterías en parking. La tripulación los rearma pasando el BAT pb a OFF y luego a AUTO. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 30 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["Abren en tierra, con BAT pb en AUTO, sin fuente principal (EXT PWR + GEN cortados) y baja tensión de batería; se rearman pasando el BAT pb a OFF y luego a AUTO","Abren en vuelo con baja tensión; se rearman solos al aterrizar","Abren siempre que se apague el APU; se rearman con EXT PWR","Abren con cualquier BAT pb en OFF; se rearman pasando a AUTO"]},"en":{"q":"The automatic battery cut-off logic on ground (parking) prevents full discharge. Under what conditions do the contactors open and how are they reset?","keys":["ground","bat","source","gen","battery","voltage"],"answer":"The automatic contactors open when: the aircraft is on ground, BAT pb in AUTO, the main source is cut off (EXT PWR + GEN) and battery voltage is low. This prevents draining the batteries at parking. The crew resets them by moving the BAT pb to OFF then AUTO. (FCOM DSC-24-20 · p. 30 · rev 15 MAY 25)","opts":["They open on ground, with BAT pb in AUTO, no main source (EXT PWR + GEN cut off) and low battery voltage; they reset by moving the BAT pb to OFF then AUTO","They open in flight with low voltage; they reset by themselves on landing","They open whenever the APU is shut down; they reset with EXT PWR","They open with any BAT pb OFF; they reset by going to AUTO"]}},{"sys":"ELEC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-ELEC-FCTM-006","es":{"q":"Si la tripulación establece voluntariamente la configuración eléctrica de emergencia tras un AVIONICS SMOKE, ¿en qué se diferencia el objetivo del procedimiento ECAM respecto a la pérdida de generadores?","keys":["ecam","muestra","procedimiento","especifico","objetivo","restablecer"],"answer":"Cuando la config de emergencia se establece voluntariamente por AVIONICS SMOKE, el ECAM muestra un procedimiento específico: como el piloto la ha puesto a propósito, el objetivo NO es restablecer los generadores, sino permanecer en emergencia (aislando la fuente de humo) y restablecerlos antes de aterrizar para tomar en configuración normal. (FCTM PR-AEP-SMOKE · p. 552 · rev 22 MAY 24)","opts":["El ECAM muestra un procedimiento específico cuyo objetivo NO es restablecer los generadores, sino permanecer en emergencia y restablecerlos antes de aterrizar para tomar en configuración normal","Es el mismo procedimiento en ambos casos","El objetivo es restablecer los generadores lo antes posible, igual que en la pérdida de generadores","El procedimiento obliga a mantener la configuración de emergencia hasta después del aterrizaje"]},"en":{"q":"If the crew voluntarily sets the emergency electrical configuration after an AVIONICS SMOKE, how does the ECAM procedure objective differ from a loss of generators?","keys":["ecam","shows","specific","procedure","whose","objective"],"answer":"When the emergency configuration is set voluntarily due to AVIONICS SMOKE, the ECAM shows a specific procedure: since the crew set it on purpose, the objective is NOT to restore the generators, but to remain in emergency (isolating the smoke source) and restore them before landing to land in normal configuration. (FCTM PR-AEP-SMOKE · p. 552 · rev 22 MAY 24)","opts":["The ECAM shows a specific procedure whose objective is NOT to restore the generators, but to remain in emergency and restore them before landing to land in normal configuration","It is the same procedure in both cases","The objective is to restore the generators as soon as possible, just like the loss of generators","The procedure requires keeping the emergency configuration until after landing"]}}];
    QB.push.apply(QB, window.QB_ELEC);
    if(window.console) console.log('[qbank-elec] +' + window.QB_ELEC.length + ' preguntas ELÉCTRICO bilingües');
  } catch (e) { if (window.console) console.warn('[qbank-elec] no se pudo enganchar al QB:', e); }
})();
